<i>Never gonna stop, never gonna stop</i>

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.040
<i>Ai suru kimochi wa happiness</i>

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.250
<i>You were not in pain, you were not in pain</i>

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.910
<i>Ai suru ga yue ni sadness</i>

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.950
<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.250
<i>You gonna feel so</i>

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.250
<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:52.730
Chapter 2 Will

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.160
He's the one from yesterday.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.820
Whoops!

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.940
Hey, you big brute!

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.490
You bastard!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.240
Well, I guess that's about
the best you've got.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.200
Shinpachi, I'm sparring with you
here because you asked me to!

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.120
What's with that smartass attitude?!

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.880
Uh-oh...

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.120
Wait a minute, Sanosuke!

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.290
I'm at a disadvantage if you use that!

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.720
There's no time for that in combat!

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.160
Okay, okay!

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.600
I get it, so let's just call it
quits and grab some food!

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.230
Food?!

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.640
Mr. Hijikata, are you awake?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.580
Come on, if you stay in bed forever,

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.830
mushrooms will start growing on your head.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:57.960
It's been raining nonstop since yesterday.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:05.450
I wonder if the puppy was able
to find shelter from the rain.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.580
No idea.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.990
I won't give up.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.250
You are actually a great man.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.410
You said you were going to exact revenge.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:38.210
For that purpose, could you abandon
everything, even your humanity?

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.050
Damn it...

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:51.530
Moron...

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.160
Why do you have to be so stubborn?

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.150
It's almost time for breakfast.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.910
Come on, hurry up!

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.740
Dammit, Tetsu!

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.920
He's still there?

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.800
Tetsu, you've made your point, okay?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.080
That's enough already. Let's give up.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.310
Okay?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.830
I will fear nothing, not even demons.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.790
Please turn me into a demon.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.470
You're small in all respects,

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.350
but your eyes have the mettle
of a full-fledged man.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.360
You're a lot like Soji.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.540
All right.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.910
Tetsunosuke Ichimura,

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.700
out of consideration for Soji,
I'll allow you to sign on.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.820
Really, Mr. Hijikata?!

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:40.880
Tetsu!

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:49.300
I did it, Dad, Mom, Tatsu...

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.600
Well, isn't that great?

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.290
Are we alike?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.480
I think there's someone else
he resembles much more.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.820
Oh, it seems the rain has let up.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.240
Seconds!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.830
You sure are energetic for
having been up all night.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.670
That's good!

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:30.380
Don't drink miso soup like it's sake.
Just don't.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.580
Oh, come on, it's good!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.080
You know, Tetsu,

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:39.120
I'm keeping a lid on a whole lot
of things I want to say to you.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.100
Aren't you going to sit still and
listen even for just a little bit?

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.020
Seconds!

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:47.770
Goodness gracious, you eat a lot.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:52.560
If your seniors get mad at you on account of
not being able to get seconds for supper,

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:53.910
don't say I didn't warn you.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:59.290
Miss, this food is great! I haven't
had anything this good in two years!

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.500
Really? You sure do pay
a pretty compliment.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:08.700
Because, well, the meals we used to have were
pickled radish, pickled radish, pickled radish...

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.460
Maybe dried sardines once in a while.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:12.800
Tetsu...

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.870
Guess I can't hardly cut
corners with my cooking

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.970
when we've got two such darling
things who've just signed on.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.060
Two things... Meaning me too?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.310
Here.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:25.440
All right! Thanks, Miss!

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.750
My name's Ayumu. Ayumu Yamazaki.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.860
But I don't mind if you just call me Ayu.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.650
Ayu?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.700
You're a good kid.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.620
I reckon this is what having a
kid brother's supposed to be like.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.660
You have a kid brother?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.280
Of sorts...

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:48.170
Good morning, cannon boy!

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:50.450
We came to say hi!

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.510
You remember us?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.620
Oh, here comes the noisy rabble again.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.470
Sorry about that, Ayu.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.910
Ichimura, was it?
Congratulations on getting in!

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.750
You're something else to make
Mr. Hijikata change his mind!

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.270
We were watching your match
yesterday! But man, you're small!

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.980
Who are you people?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:14.080
Oh, guess we haven't
introduced ourselves yet.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.160
I'm the Tenth Unit Captain

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.950
and the best spear fighter
in the Shinsengumi!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.700
Sanosuke Harada! 25 years old!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.120
Also known as Suicide Attempter Sanosuke!

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.250
Behold my badge of honor!

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.420
The scar from attempted seppuku!

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:32.830
Your stomach's still in banquet mode!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.790
I've gone and done it!

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:41.450
And I'm his keeper, the great
Shinpachi Nagakura.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.410
I might not look it, but I'm
the Second Unit Captain.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.620
Nice to meet you.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.600
What the hell did you just say?!

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.750
There's one more.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.370
A funny guy named Todo, but...

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.790
Well, I'm sure he'll be back eventually.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:55.610
So, the two of you both serve
directly under the Vice Commander.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:56.570
Right.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:57.030
You got it.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.740
Hey, you're...

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.920
You giant monster, how dare
you trample me yesterday?!

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.880
Trample? Did I now?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:22.430
Sorry, I just don't see anyone
who's smaller than Shinpachi!

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.100
What the hell did you say?!

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:25.930
Cool it!

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.600
I'm very sorry! He's just a brat
who doesn't know any manners.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.400
But maybe that's what worked in his favor.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.830
An ordinary brat wouldn't have
challenged Soji to a match,

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:38.000
nor would he have stuck
it out all night in the rain.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.450
That's right. I wish I could've
heard your famous line too.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.910
Well, I'm sure things will get
tougher from here on out,

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.450
but I've got high hopes for you, Shorty.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.080
Don't call me Shorty.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.330
Well, that's all we came to say.
Wanna get going?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.040
What? Me?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.760
Your daily tasks.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:57.010
We haven't explained them to you yet
because of yesterday's commotion, remember?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.590
Come on, bro, up on your feet!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.700
Please stop.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.680
Stop...

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.510
What about me?

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.100
We told you, remember?

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.680
That things are gonna get much tougher.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.750
So, about yesterday's action...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:35.250
By the time we got there,
the Second Unit had completely cleaned up.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.130
So you went out there for nothing?

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:41.970
Well, in the end, the Choshu are
just samurai from the countryside.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.000
Excuse me...

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:45.720
I...

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.950
Hey, you're the kid that
joined up this morning, right?

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.160
You sure are little!

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.480
Are we really sure about
signing on a whelp like him?

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.970
I'm fifteen years old, damn it.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.870
Hey, little guy!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.790
Which Unit are you being assigned to?

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:06.240
If you don't know, try asking Mr. Hijikata.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.500
Mr. Hijikata?

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.250
Oh, man. Mr. Hijikata's
that scary guy, right?

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.630
You're that pig!

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.220
Hey, hold it right there!

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:33.040
Mr. Hijikata...

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.410
What is it? You're in an
awfully good mood, Soji.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:39.570
Yes, when I think of how we're
getting a cute page starting today...

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:44.700
I don't remember having turned
this place into a day care center.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:48.070
And where is that brat
wandering around, anyway?

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:52.950
I believe Mr. Harada and
Mr. Nagakura went to get Tetsu.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.790
Those guys...

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:56.450
Hold it right there!

00:12:57.950 --> 00:12:59.390
Oh, and here he is, right on cue.

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:00.550
Hold it!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.010
There, there.
You bastard!

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.160
You should know better, Tetsu.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.510
A page shouldn't be wandering
around here like this.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.850
Page? You mean me?

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.870
Mr. Hijikata is growing impatient.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.850
Why don't you go make him tea or something?

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:21.240
I'm Mr. Hijikata's page?!

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.280
Hot!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.800
I spilled it.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.290
Listen to me, Tetsu.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:09.740
Being Mr. Hijikata's page isn't
something just anyone can do.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.900
It's an incredible thing.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.700
Are you listening, Tetsu?

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:20.290
I joined to become
stronger, and here I am...

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.660
serving tea!

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:26.250
Damn it! I'll serve him some mopped up tea!

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:27.840
Oh, Mr. Hijikata!

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:38.560
Why have I been assigned to be
the Vice Commander's page anyway?

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.480
He's the one who hates me the most.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:46.070
Are you scared?
What?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.200
It'll be fine.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.450
You'll be able to do it, because it's you.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:46.640
Okay, no one's looking.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.620
Be quiet!

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.450
Tatsu!

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.020
What time do you think it is?

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.950
What're you doing in here anyway?

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.620
I figured you wouldn't be
able to sleep anywhere else,

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:11.780
so I was getting it ready for you.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:13.930
That's...

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:18.440
I know. It's okay.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.200
But...

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:24.410
don't you think it's about time you
could be forgiven for letting it go?

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:12.590
Tatsu!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:20.910
That's...

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:25.610
Mr. Hijikata's room...

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:32.660
I presume you have heard this
from Mr. Nagakura and Mr. Harada,

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:35.280
but concerning the incident on
Kiyamachi Street yesterday...

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:37.540
Please take a look at this.

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.830
Yes, thank you.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.910
I see.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.660
So they did disappear
onto Oike Street after all.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:49.040
They're up to something.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:52.880
I saw the same ronin going
in and out again today.

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.250
Good work. Continue
investigating the matter...

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.140
Please wait a moment.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:20.910
<i>Who the hell is this guy?</i>

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:23.690
What is it?

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.080
Nothing, it was just a pup.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.700
<i>A pup...</i>

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.870
<i>The hell did you call me?!</i>

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:34.960
Who's a pup...?

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.910
That voice just now...

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:45.950
You know, Tetsu, if you do
any more dramatic things,

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:48.310
I seriously might not
survive trying to keep up.

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:51.230
Or did you want to give dying a try?

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:56.030
Keep it to a minimum. We don't
have any medicine for nerves here.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:57.950
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.580
I followed him, thinking
he might be a robber,

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:03.450
and I heard him talking
to the Vice Commander

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:05.410
about yesterday's incident and
people being up to something!

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:09.000
That suspicious man you saw?
That's a watcher.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.460
Watcher?

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.450
They're different from our other members,

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:14.620
and they move around gathering information.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:17.250
They're basically what you'd call spies.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:20.470
Normally, they live as other people
and don't show their faces,

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.120
so they're treated as
mystery people even here.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:24.660
Wow...

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.640
But you certainly know a lot
for them being mystery people.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:32.560
Oh, well, I cook for
everyone, so that's nothing.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:36.320
Hey, hey, could I become a watcher too?

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.370
Because...

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.870
I can't fight against
the Choshu as a page.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:42.990
Tetsu...

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.490
Could it be that you two have
a vendetta against the Choshu?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.660
They killed our parents.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.200
Of course, the Choshu Clan is known

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.330
for leading the loyalist movement
to bring down the Shogunate.

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:57.290
We were told the ones
who killed our parents

00:19:57.290 --> 00:20:00.650
were extremist exclusionists
even among the Choshu clansmen.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.580
And we thought in order
to find their murderers,

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.830
the best way would be to
join the Shinsengumi,

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:08.410
Truth

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:08.410
who work under the
Military Commissioner of Kyoto.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.290
If we joined the Shinsengumi,

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:13.160
we could get information on the
Choshu and also become stronger.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:16.160
I was casually saying it would serve
to kill two birds with one stone,

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:19.070
but it seems this guy
here took it seriously.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.280
That's boys for you.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.740
I've decided! I'll quit being a
page and become a watcher!

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.200
That's just not funny...

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.700
I mean, come on!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:35.160
There's a brat about the same age as me
doing a cool job like being a watcher,

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:38.830
while I have to serve the Vice Commander?
That's totally wrong!

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:44.090
I'll show them that I can do better
than that spiky-headed bastard!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.300
Tetsu, you moron!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.300
And his eyebrows are starting to go too!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.300
I'll bet he doesn't have
any friends, either!

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:50.850
Like hell I'll lose to a no-eyebrow
depressing guy like him!

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.800
<i>So that's it.</i>...

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:53.500
All right, starting
tomorrow, I'll be a watcher!

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.190
All right!

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:56.700
Well, since that's settled,
I'm going to sleep now!

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:58.060
Good night!

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:00.370
Oh, there he goes again
without saying thanks.

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:03.950
I'm really sorry. You treated his
wound when it's so late at night.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:07.120
It's not a bother. I was having
trouble falling asleep anyway.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.290
I don't think of him as endearing,

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:12.540
but I suppose it's natural to get mad
when someone else badmouths him.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:15.500
Please don't let it get to you.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.830
He meant no harm.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:17.660
Well, then...

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.470
A watcher?

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:32.160
He still just pisses me off!

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:34.980
It won't open!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:38.730
Damn it, Tatsu, open the door!

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:07.910
<i>Maiku o nigirishime
hitto pareedo no onpareedo</i>

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.390
<i>Hey, Jimmy, kibun wa doudai?</i>

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:15.790
<i>Suteeji orireba sasuga no jentoruman</i>

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:19.450
<i>Hey, Jimmy, kokoro mo kandai!</i>

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:23.320
<i>Jimichi ga yue ni seikatsu sae mo jimi ni</i>

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:27.290
<i>Kotsu-kotsu tsumiagemashou</i>

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:31.290
<i>Jimichi ni yume ga kanaimasu you ni</i>

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:35.120
<i>Kyou mo, Jimmy, ikimashou</i>

